# EAS uploads from the git monorepo root. Composer path packages install as
# Windows junctions under **/vendor; recreating those in the upload tarball
# fails the "Compressing project files" step. The offline mobile app does
# not need any of the Laravel apps or PHP packages.
**/vendor/

central-app/
pharmacy-app/
finance-app/
hr-app/
restaurant-app/
trial-app/
templates/
docs/
admin-docs/
ops/
contracts/
examples/
.github/
packages/
pharmacy-electron-app/
pharmacy-mobile-app/
restaurant-electron-app/

**/node_modules/
**/.expo/
**/dist/
# Each app's generated native folders (EAS runs prebuild). Only an app's own
# android/ and ios/: a local Expo module's android/ (modules/*/android, such as
# the SUNMI printer) is source and must be uploaded, or the build leaves the
# module out and the app falls back to the print dialog.
/*/android/
/*/ios/
**/android/build/
**/android/.gradle/
**/android/.cxx/
